<!-- Real itunda mark (2026-08-22, direct user identity work): replaces the old
     shield-check glyph with the "petal" shape in indigo, chosen after a full 14-shape
     x 16-color exploration pass - see the itunda-identity.html design artifact and
     project_itunda_brand_identity.md for the full derivation (indigo is not
     invented: same OKLCH hue-rotation technique Toss's own eng blog documents,
     toss.tech/article/tds-color-system-update, applied to the real itunda blue
     anchor this token held before). Two independent flat facets rather than the
     exploration artifact's full 3D gradient rendering - Android VectorDrawable
     gradients inside adaptive-icon layers render unreliably across launcher
     implementations/densities, and a flat two-tone reads just as clearly at
     launcher-icon scale (matches how Google's own apps flatten otherwise-gradient
     marks for this exact context). Right facet uses the mark's own "mid" tone
     (indigo family rm), left facet its darker "mid" counterpart (lm) - the same
     two real tones the gradient's own mid-stop uses, so this stays a true flattening
     of the real mark rather than a separately-invented icon color. Scaled to 0.60x
     and centered on (54,54), fitting inside Android's real 66dp safe-zone circle
     (108dp canvas) - verified against both a circular and squircle mask via a real
     SVG render before this file was written (rsvg-convert, not eyeballed). -->
